verifier:
I could not refute F3: the provenance claim overstates. The figures themselves are right; the record that should hold them is missing.

The A35 Results heading in audit/AUDIT_LOG.md (line 935) credits everything that follows to audit/evidence/emerging/ev_a35_surrogate_specification.csv and run 9a528268. The README section of export/excel/README.md says the surrogate was written by python/surrogate_buildings.py from that run.

What the run produces:
- I read run() and settle() in python/surrogate_buildings.py. settle() uses only SEED = 1. run() writes the 20-row specification table (the evidence file), the terms, spline-piece and mapping CSVs, the row-level parquet, and buildings_surrogate_reconciliation.csv. It prints only the specification table and the reconciliation.
- The reconciliation holds the spline and re-evaluation checks, the factor 0.99949, the bare string "530 / 502", the in-sample and held-out accuracy, new business against renewals, the reference policies, the seven-value one-feature totals, the interaction gain shares and the input hashes.
- All six output files match the sha256 recorded for run 9a528268 in audit/run_log.jsonl.

What it does not produce: none of the figures F3 lists is written by run() or appears in the evidence or reconciliation CSV. That covers:
- the seed 2 and 3 grid;
- the elevation-by-zone table and the 44%, 72% and 122% per-row figures;
- 97%, +30% and +2.6%;
- 10.8%, 5.5% and 18.8%, and 4.1% and 13.6%;
- 58 of 887;
- +0.2% and +0.3%;
- the 9/19 split of the 28 aliased dimensions and its 17/1/1 breakdown;
- 0.016;
- the renewal move of +0.6%;
- the climate tail move of 1.6%;
- the 68%, 15% and 9% shares of split gain beyond the knots.

There is no audit/exploratory/a35 folder, unlike a31 to a33, which each have one with a MANIFEST.sha256. The tests and export_excel.py do not compute these figures either. A33 states plainly which checks were done outside its archived script; A35 marks only its first-fit figures as unarchived. Its Verification bullet says an independent check recomputed every figure, but no script for that check is archived.

Recomputation: I rebuilt the final GLM as run() does. It reproduces the exported surrogate column exactly, and the rescored trees reproduce small_claim on every row. Every listed figure then came out at its stated value:
- 887 zone-5 rows, 58 of them at 2.1 m or more.
- Rows in zones 4 and 5: totals +0.22% and +0.32%, median errors 6.6% and 7.1%.
- 2025 rows with an OTHER pair: 10.76%, with median and 95th-percentile errors 5.53% and 18.84%, against 4.11% and 13.61% on the rest.
- Zone 4 elevation bands: +3.3, +3.6, +2.7, +13.0, +13.8, +14.1%. Zone 5: +12.0, +9.75, +25.7, +43.1, +45.1, +46.0%.
- Rows at 2.8 m or more moved to zone 5: median 43.8%, 95th percentile 71.6%, largest 121.7%.
- Rows moved to zone 5 that fall in an OTHER cell: 97.47%, at +30.5% in total, against +2.57% on the rest.
- Renewal move: +0.59%, with the median error going from 4.2% to 4.3%.
- Largest climate tail move: +1.55% (mean temperature at its 99.5th percentile).
- Seeds 2 and 3: the chosen candidate's error moves by +0.000085 and -0.000057, and the winner becomes 12 knots at power 1.5 and 10 knots at power 1.5 respectively.
- Rank: 530 columns, rank 502. Of the 28 aliased dimensions, 9 come from the crosses and 19 from the main terms (17 customer since, 1 campaign code, 1 discount).
- Renewal count and customer since together reach at most 0.0160 on the log scale.

One figure needs a qualification. The 68%, 15% and 9% shares reproduce only when the count is limited to split points with 2025 values on both sides, as a share of all that feature's gain (67.7%, 15.1%, 8.6%). Counting every split point instead gives 92% for wildfire index, 66% for mean temperature and 38% for dry summer index, which would break the README's "under 5%" for the other splines. That restriction is described only by the README phrase "Within the 2025 range" and is not in any archived code. It is further evidence for this finding, not an error.

So the document is wrong on provenance, not on numbers: the Results heading credits figures to the run and its evidence file that neither holds, and no script for them is archived.
